HUMAN: I need to get the proto of each friend when clicking on the GUI list entry. I can hook the list item but how do I get to the actual friend?

ASSISTANT: To get the proto of each friend when clicking on the GUI list entry, you can hook into the method that handles the click event on the list item. Once you have hooked into the method, you can access the friend's proto from the context. Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

const FriendPickerGuiController = Ditto.use("FriendPickerGuiController");
const ListItemClickMethod = FriendPickerGuiController.ListItemClickMethod; // Replace ListItemClickMethod with the actual method name that handles the click event

ListItemClickMethod.attach({
  onEnter: function (args) {
    const listItem = args[0]; // Assuming the first argument is the list item
    const friendProto = listItem.friendProto; // Replace 'friendProto' with the actual field name in the list item that holds the friend's proto

    console.log("Clicked friend's proto:", friendProto);
  },
});
Make sure to replace ListItemClickMethod and friendProto with the actual method and field names from the provided code snippets.

